  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Npc155187 and Neuropilin-2 through a series of target interactions. Path_252029 links Npc155187 to Leukocyte antigen CD37, which is targeted by 1-Aminopropan-2-Ol, a compound that in turn targets Neuropilin-2. Path_252030 and Path_252031 both connect Npc155187 to WI-38, which is targeted by Hederagenin 28-O-Beta-D-Glucopyranosyl Ester and 5,10-Dimethoxy-2,2-Dimethylpyrano[3,2-G]Chromen-8-One, both of which also target Neuropilin-2. These pathways collectively indicate that Npc155187 may act as a mediator in the activation or regulation of Neuropilin-2 through multiple distinct molecular mechanisms. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Npc155187 and Neuropilin-2, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated. The presence of multiple target compounds targeting Neuropilin-2 suggests that Npc155187 may function as a central node in a complex regulatory network involving various signaling pathways.",
